--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SURFACE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DatePresetChips is the web quick-select chip row for date ranges (web/src/components/forms/DatePresetChips.tsx).
The web component renders a role="group" container (aria-label = t('date.preset.label', 'Quick date range'))
holding one shared <Button> chip per preset id — filtered from the static DATE_PRESETS table and defaulting to
DEFAULT_PRESET_IDS (['today','7d','30d','mtd','ytd','all']). The active preset (p.id === activeId) renders as a
primary chip with aria-pressed; the rest render as ghost chips. Clicking a chip resolves the preset's inclusive
range from the local calendar day and calls onSelect({ id, start, end }) with ISO YYYY-MM-DD strings.

It is presentational: the web source consumes only useTranslation and the static preset table — NO data hooks,
charts, maps, and NO loading/error/stale/offline branches. The honest native union is therefore the two states
the catalogue can yield — the populated chip row (Populated) and, when the supplied ids resolve to no presets
(the web's empty group), a friendly empty surface (Empty, never a blank box). Fabricating loading/error/stale/
offline chrome the web source lacks would be parity drift, so — per the SuggestedPrompts / Delta presentational-
surface precedent — none was invented. Evidence is in the doc-comments.

Reuse / DRY: the surface binds the existing canonical native port of the web preset table,
TeslaSync.App.Core.Forms.DatePresets / DatePreset / DateRange (id filtering, range maths), instead of
re-porting it. The web Button maps to the shared TsButton (Variant Primary for the active chip = web
'primary'; Variant Subtle for the rest = web 'ghost'); the empty surface maps to the shared TsEmptyState; the
wrapping row reuses the house ChipWrapPanel flow-panel pattern (base WinUI ships no wrap panel).

Native decomposition (flat file layout, matching the Delta / QueryError sibling surfaces):
  - DatePresetChips.Model.cs     DatePresetChipSize, DatePresetChipsState (Populated/Empty), DatePresetSelection
                                 (web DatePresetSelection), DatePresetChipItem, DatePresetChipsDisplay,
                                 Registration (Slug "DatePresetChips"; i18n keys translation.date.preset.label /
                                 translation.common.noData / translation.<preset> ; ISO formatter),
                                 Projection (id filter + localize + active flag + click-time range Resolve),
                                 PII-safe DatePresetChipsDiagnostics (view.opened + preset.selected with the
                                 fixed non-PII id token).
  - DatePresetChips.Source.cs    IDatePresetChipsSource + DatePresetChipsSource (P1/S8 seam: PresetIds, ActiveId,
                                 Size, AriaLabel; injectable Today clock = the web new Date() local day; null ids
                                 fall back to DEFAULT_PRESET_IDS, empty ids preserved so Empty is reachable).
  - DatePresetChips.ViewModel.cs DatePresetChipsViewModel — observes the source, projects the Display, raises
                                 INotifyPropertyChanged; Select(id) resolves the range and raises Selected (web
                                 onSelect); Reload() re-resolves labels on language change; idempotent Dispose.
  - DatePresetChips.cs           DatePresetChips : ContentControl — wrapping ChipWrapPanel of TsButton chips /
                                 TsEmptyState; raises PresetSelected; transparent? no — a Group automation peer
                                 carrying the localized aria-label (web role="group"); each chip is a
                                 PresetChipButton exposing the UIA Toggle pattern so Narrator announces the active
                                 chip's pressed state (web aria-pressed); emits view.opened once on Loaded;
                                 marshals view-model changes to the UI thread.

i18n: every label resolves through the P1/S10 ILocalizer facade. Each key the web source uses has a matching
catalog entry (verified in apps/shared/i18n/catalog/en.json and apps/windows/Strings/en/Resources.resw):
translation.date.preset.label ("Quick date range"), translation.date.preset.{today,last7,last30,last90,
yesterday,mtd,qtd,ytd,lastMonth,last1y,all}, and translation.common.noData (the friendly empty message). No
hardcoded English in native code.

