PRE-EXISTING BLOCKER REPAIRED (tightly coupled to this task)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The committed apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj did NOT load at HEAD: it had TWO
<Project> roots (lines 1-1317 and 1318-2575, the second prefixed with a stray BOM), and the first root's header
was a stack of merged regeneration comments — one <!-- opener but five --> closers — leaving non-whitespace
#text children of <Project>. This is the recurrence the file's own INVARIANT documents (the .gitattributes
merge=union strategy re-concatenating it into multiple roots), and it fails MSBuild load with MSB4025 / MSB4067,
making the whole-solution build red at baseline independent of this surface. Because this surface's WinUI-free
sources must be Compile-linked there, it was repaired per the file's own invariant.

The two roots had DIVERGED — neither was a superset (root1 uniquely carried QueryError / RateLimitBanner /
ReleaseNotes / RequiresAuth / Spinner / SuspenseProgressBoundary; root2 uniquely carried ReloadPrompt /
SectionErrorBoundary / SkipToContent) — so a truncate-to-one-root repair would have silently dropped sibling
surfaces' links and broken their tests. Repair: regenerated as exactly ONE <Project> root with a single clean
header comment, the PropertyGroup, the three non-Compile ItemGroups (PackageReference, ProjectReference, Content
— all 8 items preserved), and a single case-insensitive ordinal path-sorted, Include-deduplicated Compile
ItemGroup = the union of both roots' links plus this surface's 3 new headless links.

The result was VERIFIED to exactly equal the union of every Microsoft.UI-free .cs on disk under
dashboard-widgets/, feature-views/, misc-surfaces/, modals-dialogs/ and shared-surfaces/:
  1147 pre-existing WinUI-free sources + 3 new DatePresetChips headless sources = 1150.
  DISK_HEADLESS=1150 == INCLUDE_SET=1150 (DIFF=0; zero stale links, zero misclassifications).
The bare WinUI view DatePresetChips.cs (Microsoft.UI-referencing) is correctly excluded.
Post-write XML check: STRAY_TEXT_CHILDREN=0, <Project> roots=1, PropertyGroups=1, ItemGroups=4, Compile=1150,
comment markers balanced (<!--=2, -->=2). LF, no BOM.

